  "id": "ideomotor-principle",
  "term": "ideomotor principle",
  "definition": "The ideomotor principle is the idea that actions are guided by anticipating their sensory consequences. In this view, expecting a desired effect can call up the movement patterns that have previously produced that effect, helping control voluntary, goal-directed behavior.",
